    "ls|LS17_S3_U_331": " \n \n                                  \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n \n331\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n4\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY\n,\n \n20\n20\n \n \nREDUCED ENROL\nMENT UNDER PMFBY\n \n \n331.\n \n \nSHRI ABU HASEM KHAN CHOWDHURY\n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n   \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \u0000कसान क\u0000याण मं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \n \nwhether the number of insured farmers under the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana \n(PMFBY) has reduced over the last two years;\n \n \n(b)\n \n \nif so, the reasons for the fall in the number of insured farmers;\n \n \n(\nc) \n \nthe number of farmers insured under PMFBY from the year 2016 to 2019, year\n-\nwise and \nState\n-\nwise; \n \n \n(d)\n \n \nthe findings of all the joint review missions conducted by the Ministry on PMFBY;\n \n \n(e)\n \n \nthe amount incurred by the Union Government towards paying th\ne premiums and \nliabilities, year\n-\nwise and State\n-\nwise;\n \n \n \n(f) \n \nwhether the Ministry had invited suggestions from the stakeholders in the year 2019 to \nmake the scheme more effective; and \n \n \n(g)\n \n \nif so, the details of the changes made in the policy after receiv\ning these suggestions?\n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nM\nINISTER \n \nOF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं\n \n\u0000कसान\n \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n \n    \n(\nSHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR\n)\n \n \n(a)  to (c)\n:\n \n \nNo Sir.  \nThough the coverage during 2\nnd\n \nyear of implementation i.e. 2017\n-\n18 of Pradhan \nMantri Fasal Bi\nma Yojana (PMFBY) slightly decreased due to announcement of loan waiver schemes by \nsome State and making Aadhar compulsory for de\n-\nduplication in coverage, but due to the improved \nfeatures of the scheme introduced by the Government, coverage has showing inc\nreased \ntrends\n \nin 2018\n-\n19.  \n \n \nState\n-\nwise and Year\n-\nwise details of coverage of farmer applicants since inception of the scheme \nin Kharif 2016 till 2018\n-\n19 are \nannexed\n.\n \n(d)\n: \n \nNo specific joint review mission has been set up by the Government for implementatio\nn of \nPMFBY.  \nHowever, Government undertakes close monitoring of the scheme on day to day basis through \nw\neekly Video Conferences with States/insurance companies/ financial institutions, one to one meetings \non State specific issues with States and insurance \ncompanies concerned, weekly meeting of insurance \ncompanies, quarterly review meetings with all stakeholders. Integrated crop insurance portal also \nprovides an effective real\n-\ntime monitoring tool for all stake holders.  Further, Government also works to \nimp\nrove the implementation of PMFBY operational system with stringent seasonality discipline for all \nimplementing stakeholders to ensure faster insurance services and relief to farmers with prompt claim \nsettlement\n.\n \n(e)\n:\n \n \nState\n-\nwise and year\n-\nwise details of Go\nvernment of India’s share in premium subsidy under \nPMFBY are \nAnnexed\n.\n \n \n(f)\n: \n  \n \nThe \nGovernment\n \nhas recently revised the Operational Guidelines of the scheme with effect from \nRabi 2018\n-\n19 season.  Inviting of suggestions from various stakeholders and revisio\nns/ improvements in \nthe crop insurance schemes is a continuous process and decisions on suggestions/representations are \ntaken from time to time after consultation with various stakeholders.   Accordingly, suggestions for \nrevamping of PMFBY have been invite\nd from the stakeholders.\n \n\n \nA\nNNEXURE\n \nState\n-\nwise details of total number of farmer applicant insured and Government of India’s \nshare in Premium subsidy under Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) for the year \n2016\n-\n17 to 2018\n-\n19\n \n \nState/UT Name\n \nTotal Number\n \nof Farmers Insured\n 