    "ls|LS17_S3_U_374": " Government of India \nMinistry of Youth Affairs & Sports \nDepartment of Sports \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 374 \nTO BE ANSWERD ON 19.03.2020 \n \nCommonwealth Shooting and Archery Championships \n \n*374. SHRI SHRIRANG APPA BARNE:  \n SHRI BIDYUT BARAN MAHATO: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) whether India is going to host Commonwealth Shooting and \nArchery Championships in January, 2022 and if so, the details \nthereof;  \n(b) whether all the stakeholders have been consulted in  this regard, \nif so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;  \n(c) the details of infrastructure facilities required for the said events \nalong with the time -frame set for completion of these infrastructure \nfacilities;  \n(d) the details of estim ated funds required to develop necessary \nsports infrastructure facilities and organize the said games in the \ncountry; and  \n(e) whether the said step is likely to provide more opportunities for \ncommonwealth athletes to compete on the world stage and if so, \nthe details thereof? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n[SHRI KIREN RIJIJU] \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n**** \n  \n\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF THE \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 374 FOR REPLY ON \n19.03.2020 ASKED BY SHRI SHRIRANG APPA BARNE  AND SHRI \nBIDYUT BARAN MAHATO REGARDING COMMONWEALTH SHOOTING \nAND ARCHERY CHAMPIONSHIPS \n \n(a) & (b) Shooting and Archery are not compulsory sports under \nthe Commonwealth Games Federation (CGF) Constitution and were \nnot included in the Birmingham 2022 Commonwealth Games. \nHowever, the Government has also constantly taken up the issue of \ninclusion of the ‘Shooting’ in the Birmingham 2022 Commonwealth \nGames with the CGF, Orga nizing Committee of Birmingham \nCommonwealth Games 2022 as also with the concerned authority in \nUK Government. With the combined efforts of this Ministry, the \nIndian Olympic Association (IOA) and the National Rifle Association \nof India, the CGF has agreed t o hold ‘Shooting’ and ‘Archery’ \nChampionships in India in advance of the Birmingham 2022 \nCommonwealth Games with the legitimacy of medals of these \nevents as part of the final tally for the XXII edition of the \nCommonwealth Games. These events will be held i n Chandigarh in \nJanuary 2022.  \n(c) & (d) While seeking in -principle approval of this Ministry IOA \nhas indicated approximate estimated cost of Rs.10.00 crore and \nRs.3.50 crore towards organising ‘Shooting’ and ‘Archery’ events, \nrespectively, in India apart from the venue / infrastructure facilities. \nCompetition venue which include Shooting ranges of 50 metres, 25 \nmetres, 10 metres, etc. and Archery field for Recurve and Compound \nevents would be required for the Shooting and Archery events. \nAccording to Natio nal Rifle Association of India , UT Administration \nof Chandigarh is on its own in the process of upgrading the existing \nshooting ranges and facilities to the international standard and the \ntentative time frame for completion is 12 months  and the same \nfacilities would be used for Commonwealth Shooting Championship \n2022. \n(e) Hosting of  Commonwealth Shooting and Archery \nChampionships would provide opportunities to the Indian athletes to \ncompete in an international event at home-ground.  \n*** ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_375": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 375 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MARCH 19, 2020 \n \nSMART CITIES IN GOA  \n \nNO. 375. SHRI COSME FRANCISCO CAITANO SARDINHA  : \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be p leased to \nstate: \n(a)  the names of the cities in Goa selected among the major 100 cities \nin the country by the Government under the Smart Ci ties Mission \n(SCM) along with the phases in which these cities h ave been \nselected;  \n(b)  the names of cities where work has been starte d after allocation of \nbudget under the said Mission, State-wise;  \n(c)  whether requisite budget was allocated for Pan aji city also after its \nselection for development as smart city under the s aid Mission and \nif so, the funds allocated and spent so far thereon  along with the \nperiod during which such funds were allocated; and  \n(d)  whether the work in Panaji city has almost sta lled due to the \nadministrative laxity? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n(SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n\n                                                    STATEMENT \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY OF PARTS (a) to (d) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *375 FOR ANSWER ON 19.03 .2020 \nREGARDING “SMART CITIES IN GOA”. \n \n \n(a) to (d) Panaji Smart City in Goa was selected in  Fast Track Round of \nthe Smart Cities Challenge in May 2016. \nAll 100 Smart Cities in the country have already st arted \nimplementing their Smart City Proposals. The State- wise list of 100 \nSmart Cities is given in Annexure-I. \nSo far, Government of India has released Rs. 196 cr ore for the \nPanaji Smart City, of which Rs. 106 crore has been utilized by the \nSmart City. \nOut of total 42 projects worth Rs. 1,556.4 crore in  Panaji Smart City, \n4 projects worth Rs. 43.6 crore have been tendered,  9 projects \nworth Rs. 333.5 crore have been grounded and 9 proj ects worth Rs. \n14.7 crore have been completed.  \n \n***** \n \n  \n\n \nAnnexure-I in reply to parts (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha Starred Question \nNo.375* for 19.03.2020 regarding Smart Cities in Goa by  \nShri Cosme Francisco Caitano Sardinha, Hon’ble MP. \n \nState/Union Territory(UT)-wise list of 100 Smart Cities  \n \nSl. \nNo. \nName of State/UT Smart Cities \n1. Andaman & Nicobar \nIslands \n1. Port Blair \n2. Andhra Pradesh 1. Visakhapatnam \n2. Tirupati \n3. Kakinada \n4.Amaravati \n3. Arunachal Pradesh 1.Pasighat \n2.Itanagar \n4. Assam 1. Guwahati \n5. Bihar 1. Muzaffarpur \n2. Bhagalpur \n3. Patna \n4.Biharsharif \n6. Chandigarh 1. Chandigarh \n7. Chhattisgarh 1. Raipur \n2. Bilaspur \n3. Atal Nagar (erstwhile Naya \nRaipur) \n8. Daman & Diu 1.Diu \n9. Dadra & Nagar Haveli 1.Silvassa \n10. Delhi 1. New Delhi Municipal Council  \n11. Goa 1. Panaji \n12. Gujarat 1. Gandhinagar \n2. Ahmedabad \n3. Surat \n4. Vadodara \n5. Rajkot \n6. Dahod \n13. Haryana 1. Karnal \n2. Faridabad \n14. Himachal Pradesh 1.Dharamshala \n\n2.Shimla \n15. Jammu & Kashmir 1.Jammu \n2.Srinagar \n16. Jharkhand 1. Ranchi \n17. Karnataka 1. Mangaluru \n2. Belagavi \n3. Shivamogga \n4. Hubballi-Dharwad \n5. Tumakuru \n6. Davanegere \n7. Bengaluru \n18. Kerala 1.Kochi \n2.Thiruvananthapuram \n19. Lakshadweep 1.Kavaratti \n20. Madhya Pradesh 1. Bhopal \n2. Indore \n3. Jabalpur \n4. Gwalior \n5. Sagar \n6. Satna \n7. Ujjain \n21. Maharashtra 1.Pimpri-Chinchwad \n2.Nashik \n3.Thane \n4.Solapur \n5.Nagpur \n6.Kalyan-Dombivali \n7.Aurangabad \n8.Pune \n22. Manipur 1. Imphal \n23. Meghalaya 1.Shillong \n24. Mizoram 1. Aizawl \n25. Nagaland 1. Kohima \n26. Odisha 1. Bhubaneshwar \n2. Rourkela \n27. Puducherry 1. Puducherry \n28. Punjab 1. Ludhiana \n2. Jalandhar \n3. Amritsar \n\n29. Rajasthan 1. Jaipur \n2. Udaipur \n3. Kota \n4. Ajmer \n30. Sikkim 1.Namchi \n2.Gangtok \n31. Tamil Nadu 1. Tiruchirapalli \n2. Tirunelveli \n3. Thanjavur, \n4.Tiruppur, \n5. Salem, \n6. Vellore, \n7. Coimbatore, \n8. Madurai, \n9. Thoothukudi \n10. Chennai \n11.Erode \n32. Telangana 1. Karimnagar \n2. Greater Warangal \n33. Tripura 1. Agartala \n34. Uttar Pradesh 1. Aligarh \n2. Jhansi \n3. Kanpur \n4. Prayagraj (erstwhile \nAllahabad) \n5. Lucknow \n6. Varanasi \n7. Agra \n8.Bareilly \n9.Moradabad \n10.Saharanpur \n35. Uttarakhand 1. Dehradun \n36. West Bengal 1. New Town Kolkata \n Total 100 \n \n \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_376": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 376 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 04TH FEBRUARY, 2020/MAGHA 15, 1941 (SAKA) \n \nPREPARATION OF NPR \n \n376.  SHRI MANISH TEWARI: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the persons whose citizenship is not doubtful are presumed to be \nIndian Citizens under the Registration of Citizens and Issue of National Identity \nCards Rules, 2003, Rule 4, sub-rule 4 which provides that when NPR is being \nprepared particulars of such individuals, whose Citizenship is doubtful, shall be \nentered by the Local Registrar with appropriate remark in the Population Register \nfor further enquiry and in case of doubtful citizenship, the individual or the family \nshall be informed in a specified proforma immediately after the verification \nprocess is over; and \n \n(b) whether Rule 6 which provides that (1) The Registrar General of Citizen \nRegistration shall, by order, notify the date on which the National Register of \nIndian Citizens shall be initialized throughout the country. (2) The order made \nunder sub-rule (1) may provide for the initialization period specifed by the \nRegistrar General of Citizen Registration for establishment of the National \nRegister of Indian Citizens. (3) Every individual must get himself registered with \nthe Local Registrar of Citizen Registration during the period of initialization as \nspecified under sub-rule (2) contradicts Rule 4 and reconciliation and \nharmonisation is required? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n(a): During the exercise of updation of National Population Register (NPR), no \nverification is done to find individuals whose citizenship is doubtful. \n(b): Till now, the Government has not taken any decision to prepare National \nRegister of Indian Citizens (NRIC) at the National level.  Rule 6 of the Citizenship \n(Registration of Citizens and Issue of National Identity Cards) Rules, 2003 does \nnot contradict Rule 4.  \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_377": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 377 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2020 \nBHARAT NIRMAN YOJANA \n \n377.  DR. RAMAPATI RAM TRIPATHI: \n \nWill the Minister of  RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of work being done/schemes being r un in various States under Bharat \nNirman Yojana; \n(b)  whether roads have been constructed in Uttar P radesh under the scheme; \n(c)  if so, the details thereof; and \n(d)  the details of funds allocated, released and s pent for the development of rural \nroads and construction of houses in rural areas dur ing the last three years and \nthe current year, State and year-wise? \n \n \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n \n(a) to (d): The Ministry of Rural Development is no t implementing Bharat Nirman Yojana at \npresent. The first and second phases of Bharat Nirm an were in operation from 2005-06 to \n2008-09 and 2009-10 to 2013-14 respectively. Funds were released directly by the \nconcerned Ministries to State implementing agencies  or State Governments for development \nof roads, construction of houses and supply of drinking water in rural areas. \n \nPradhan Mantri Gram Sadak Yojana (PMGSY) is a one-t ime special intervention of \nGovernment of India to provide rural connectivity, by way of a single all-weather road, to \nthe eligible unconnected habitations in the core ne twork with a population of 500 persons \nand above in plain areas and 250 persons and above in Special Category States (Arunachal \nPradesh, Assam, Manipur, Meghalaya, Mizoram, Nagala nd, Sikkim, Tripura, Himachal \nPradesh, Jammu and Kashmir and Uttarakhand), the De sert Areas (as identified in the \nDistrict Development Programme), the Tribal (Schedu le V) areas and Selected Tribal and \nBackward districts as identified by the Ministry of Home Affairs/NITI Aayog on the basis of \ncensus, 2001. In the critical Left Wing Extremism ( LWE) affected blocks (as identified by \nMHA), additional relaxation has been given to conne ct habitations with population of 100 \npersons and above. Subsequently, new intervention/v erticals for upgradation of rural roads \n\nunder PMGSY-II and providing all-weather road conne ctivity with necessary culverts and \ncross-drainage structure to 44 districts in Left Wi ng Extremism Affected Areas, which are \ncritical from security and communication point of v iew have been included under the ambit \nof the Scheme.  \n  \nIn Uttar Pradesh under PMGSY, 18,566 road works mea suring a length of 58,493.513 km \nwere sanctioned upto 30 \nth  January, 2020; out of which 18,439 road works with  a road length \nof 56,314.573 km have been completed upto 30 th  January, 2020. \nUnder the PMGSY, details of the funds allocated, re leased and utilized during the last three \nyears and current year, State-wise including Uttar Pradesh is as per Annexure-I. \nUnder Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yojana – Gramin (PMAY-G) , rural households are identified \nas beneficiaries based on housing deprivation param eters as per Socio-Economic and Caste \nCensus (SECC) 2011 data. Accordingly, all household s who are houseless or living in Zero, \nOne or Two room Kuccha house (both wall and roof be ing Kutcha), subject to exclusion \ncriteria, as per SECC-2011 data, are provided assis tance for construction of house under \nPMAY-G. An assistance of Rs.1.20 lakh in plains and  Rs.1.30 lakhs in hilly states, difficult \nareas and IAP districts is provided to the benefici aries. Under PMAY-G, details of funds \nallocated, released and utilized during the last th ree years and current year, State-wise \nincluding to Uttar Pradesh is given as Annexure-II . \n \n****** \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (d) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 377 TO BE ANSWERED \nON 04.02.2020 REGARDING Bharat Nirman Yojana \n \nFunds allocated/released 