����������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������\n�\n����������������������������������������������������� �������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������ ���� ������� ��������� ����� ������� ���� �������� �������� ����� ���������� ��� ������� �� ������ �������� ����\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������\n�\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������ ������������������� �����������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n����������������������������������������������������������\n\n�",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_415": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 415 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 4TH FEBRUARY, 2020/ MAGHA 15, 1941 \n(SAKA) \n \nINCIDENTS OF ACID ATTACKS \n \n415.   DR. DNV SENTHILKUMAR S.: \n           SHRI SHRINIWAS PATIL: \n           SHRI SUNIL DATTATRAY TATKARE: \n           DR. AMOL RAMSING KOLHE: \n           SHRI KULDEEP RAI SHARMA: \n           SHRIMATI SUPRIYA SULE: \n           DR. SUBHASH RAMRAO BHAMRE: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the current system to prevent the incidents of acid \nattack on women is inefficient and as a result, the Government \nhas not been able to achieve targeted success in checking the \nsaid incidents and if so, the corrective steps taken by the \nGovernment in this regard; \n \n(b) the number of acid attack victims that have been provided free \nmedical treatment by the Government and private hospitals as \nmandated by Section 166B of the Indian Penal Code, hospital-\nwise; \n \n(c) whether cases of violation of the said Section have come to \nthe notice of the Government since insertion of this Section and if \nso, the details thereof along with the action taken against such \nviolators; \n \n(d) whether the Government has provided employment in \nGovernment institutions/department to acid attack survivors; \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof along with the number of cases of \ndiscrimination related to work/salary registered by acid attack \nsurvivors during each of the last three years and the steps taken \nby the Government for their redressal; \n \n \n\n \n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.415 FOR 04.02.2020 \n \n \n(f) whether the Government has set up rehabilitation centres for \nacid attack victims, if so, the total number of rehabilitation \ncentres functioning to help such victims and the steps taken to \nincrease the number of rehabilitation centres in the country, \nState-wise; and \n \n(g) the other steps taken by the Government to enforce strict \nregulation for the sale of acid to prevent acid attacks in the \ncountry? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a): ‘Police’ and ‘Public Order’ are State subjects under the \nSeventh Schedule to the Constitution of India. The responsibilities \nto maintain law and order, protection of life and property of the \ncitizens rest with the respective State Governments. The State \nGovernments are competent to deal with such offences under the \nextant provisions of laws.  \nHowever, the Ministry of Home Affairs has issued a \ncomprehensive Advisory on 20thApril 2015 on taking steps to \nimplement the provisions of Indian Penal Code (IPC), expediting \ncases of Acid Attack, and to provide treatment and compensation \nto victims. This advisory is available on www.mha.gov.in. Ministry \nof Health and Family Welfare has also issued an advisory dated \n20th May, 2015 stating that no acid attack victim will be denied \ntreatment by any hospital, public or private.  \n\n \n-3- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.415 FOR 04.02.2020 \n(b) to (e): No such data is maintained centrally.  \n \n(f): The Government of India is implementing “One Stop Centre \n(OSC)” and ''Universalisation of Women Helpline (WHL)” schemes. \nOSC aims to facilitate women affected by violence with a range of \nintegrated services  \n \nunder one roof such as police facilitation, medical aid, providing \nlegal aid and legal counselling, psycho-social counselling, \ntemporary shelter etc. ''Universalisation of Women Helpline” \nscheme through the short code 181 provides 24 hours emergency \nand non-emergency response to women affected by violence, both \nin public and private spaces by linking them with appropriate \nauthorities such as Police, One Stop Centre, Hospital, Legal \nServices etc. WHL also supports women in distress with rescue \nvan and counselling services in addition to providing information \nabout women welfare schemes and programs across the country. \nFurther, the Ministry of Women and Child Development is also \nadministering Swadhar Greh Scheme for relief and rehabilitation \nof women in difficult circumstances, including the victims of acid \nattack. \n \n \n\n-4- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.415 FOR 04.02.2020 \n(g): The Ministry of Home Affairs has circulated the Model \nPoison Rules on 30th Aug 2013 to all States/UTs for notifying the \nsame to regulate the sale of acid in respective State/UT. Details \nof this advisory is available at www.mha.gov.in. \nAs per Section 166B of IPC (read with Section 357C of Code \nof Criminal Procedure (Cr. P.C.)), no acid attack victim will be \ndenied treatment by any hospital, public or private, under any \npretext and erring hospital/ clinic  violating  the  legislative  \nprovisions  is  punishable  with  \nimprisonment up to one year or fine or both. Section 357C of Cr. \nP.C. also provides that free treatment is to be provided to the acid \nattack victims. Section 357A of Cr. P.C. provides that \ncompensation under Victim Compensation Scheme is to be paid \nto the victims. Section 357B of Cr.P.C. further provides that \ncompensation payable under section 357A shall be in addition to \nthe payment of fine to victim. \n Further, pursuant to the Hon’ble Supreme Court’s order \ndated 11.05.2018 in the WP(C) 565/ 2012 - Nipun Saxena Vs. Union \nof India, National Legal Services Authority (NALSA) has \nformulated the revised scheme enhancing the compensation to be \ngiven to Women Victims/Survivors of Sexual Assault/ other crimes. \nThe scheme also covers the cases of acid attacks. The scheme  \n\n-5- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.415 FOR 04.02.2020 \nwas circulated by Ministry of Women & Child Development on \n18.05.2018 and again by Ministry of Home Affairs on 28.06.2018 to \nall States/UTs for compliance.  \nIn addition, under the Prime Minister’s Relief Fund Rs. One \nlakh as compensation is also being provided by the Prime Minister \nOffice to the acid attacks victim since 08-10-2016. \n \n****** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_416": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 416 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 23.03.2020 \n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT IN ALL SECTORS \n \n*416.  SHRI PARBATBHAI SAVABHAI PATEL:  \n SHRI NARANBHAI KACHHADIYA: \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Ministry has any proposal to initi ate skill development in all  \n the sectors;   \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n(c)  whether the Ministry is focusing its attention  on preparing a capable  \n taskforce for the prospective information technolo gy hardware industry; \n(d)  if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e)  the details of the steps taken to facilitate l oan availability for skilled   \n persons? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF MINISTRY OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP  \n(DR. MAHENDRA NATH PANDEY)  \n \n(a) to (e) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n  \n\n \n \n \nSTATEMENT TO BE LAID ON THE TABLE OF LOK SABHA IN R ESPECT OF \nPARTS (a) to (e) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *416 FOR 23 RD  \nMARCH 2020 REGARDING “SKILL DEVELOPENT IN ALL SECTO RS”.  \n \nIn pursuance of the National Policy on Skill Develo pment and Entrepreneurship \n2015,  the Government has been promoting establishm ent of Sector Skill Councils \n(SSCs) under the aegis of National Skill Developmen t Corporation (NSDC) so as to \nensure that skill development efforts being made by  all stakeholders in different \nsectors are in accordance with actual needs of indu stry. SSCs are industry-led \nbodies  responsible for creating Occupational Stand ards, developing competency \nframework, conducting  Training of  the Trainers’ P rogrammes, affiliation of \nVocational Training Institutes, conducting skill ga p studies in their respective sectors \nand most importantly assessment and certification o f trainees on the curriculum \naligned to National Skill Qualification Framework ( NSQF). Presently there are 37 \nfunctional  Sector Skill Councils covering all the priority sectors, sectors with large \nworkforce and unorganized sectors. A  list thereof  is at Annexure.  \n \nElectronic Sector Skill Council of India (ESSCI) has been set up in the domain of \nElectronics & Hardware. Thrust of the Council is on  establishing an effective and \nefficient ecosystem for development and imparting o f outcome oriented skills for the \nelectronics systems, design and manufacturing indus try (ESDM) including relevant \ncurriculum, courses, information database, delivery  system, standardization, \naccreditation and certification processes to enhanc e the employability of the Indian \nworkforce globally. The Council has trained 2.83 la kh persons out of which 1.12 lakh \npersons have been placed during 2017-18 to 2019-20.  Further, the Ministry through \nits Craftsmen Training Scheme (CTS) has been provid ing long term vocational \ntraining in 137 NSQF compliant trades in 26 sectors  including Electronics & \nHardware in 15,697 Industrial Training Institutes ( ITIs) across the country. Skill \nCourses have been designed leveraging new age techn ology to meet the \nrequirement of Industry 4.0.  and new age courses s uch as Internet of Things (IoT), \nSmart Agriculture, Geo informatics assistant, Aeron autical Structure & Equipment \nFitter, Drone, Solar Technician, Technician Mechatr onics etc have been introduced \nin National Skill Training Institutes (NSTIs) and ITIs. \n \nSkill Loan Scheme of the Government being operated by Public Sector Banks \nprovides loan  facility to aspirants wanting to do skill development courses aligned to \nNSQF  in any ITIs, Polytechnics or in a school reco gnised by Central or State \nEducation Boards or in a college affiliated to reco gnised university, training partners \naffiliated to National Skill Development Corporatio n (NSDC) Sector Skill Councils, \nState Skill Development  Missions, State Skill Corp oration etc. Amount of loan \nranges from Rs. 5,000/- to Rs.1,50, 000/- depending  on the course with an interest \nrate of 11% to 12% and repayment schedule of 3 to 7  years. Loan is sanctioned \nwithout any processing fee or collateral security o r third-party guarantee.  Further, \nNSDC, through various programmes and initiatives, e ndeavours to provide support \nto trainees and training partners to facilitate sel f-employment / entrepreneurship. It \nhas partnered with various Government Agencies and Non-Government \norganisations for extending benefits such as Mudra Loans, Entrepreneurship \nSupport among others to the skilled candidates. It is also helping in creating capacity \nand strengthening placement cells of the training p roviders to encourage \nentrepreneurship. \n                \n \n \n\n \n \n \nAnnexure \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to LSSQ No. 416 to be  answered on 23.03.2020 asked by SSHRI \nPARBATBHAI SAVABHAI PATEL and SHRI NARANBHAI KACHHA DIYA regarding ‘SKILL \nDEVELOPMENT IN ALL SECTORS’. \n \nThe list of 37 functional Sector Skill Councils (SSCs)  \n \nS. No. Sector Name of the SSC \n1 Automotive Automotive Skills Development Council \n2 Retail Retailers Association’s Skill Council of India \n3 IT-ITeS IT-ITeS  Sector Skill Council \n4 Media Media & Entertainment Skills Council \n5 Rubber, Chemical & Petro-\nChemical \nRubber, Chemical & Petrochemical Sector Skill Council \n6 Healthcare  Healthcare Sector Skill Council \n7 Gems & Jewellery  Gems & Jewellery Skill Council of India \n8 Electronics & Hardware  Electronic Sector Skill Council of India \n9 Agriculture  Agriculture Skill Council of India \n10 Telecom  Telecom Sector Skill Council of India  \n11 BFSI  Banking, Financial Services & Insurance (BFSI) Sect or Skill \nCouncil of India \n12 Leather Leather Sector Skill Council \n13 Food Processing Food Industry Capacity & Skill Initiative \n14 Logistics Logistics Skill Council \n15 Plumbing Indian Plumbing Skills Council \n16 Capital Goods Capital Goods Skill Council \n17 Construction Construction Skill Development Council of India \n18 Life Sciences Life Sciences Sector Skill Development Council \n19 Aviation & AeroSpace Aviation & Aerospace Sector Skill Council \n20 Iron & Steel Indian Iron & Steel Sector Skill Council \n21 Power Power Sector Skill Council \n22 Mining  Skill Council for Mining Sector \n23 Textiles & Handlooms Textile Sector Skill Council \n24 Apparels  Apparel, Made-up & Home Furnishing  Sector Skill Council \n25 Beauty & Wellness  Beauty & wellness Sector Skill Council \n26 Handicrafts  Handicrafts & carpets Sector Skill Council \n27 Tourism & Hospitality  Tourism & Hospitality Skill Council \n28 Infrastructure Equipment  Infrastructure Equipment Skill Council \n29 Sports  Sports, Physical Education, Fitness and Leisure Sec tor Skill \nCouncil \n30 Oil & Gas Hydro Carbon Sector Skill Council \n31 Coating & Painting Paints and Coatings Skill Council \n32 Green Jobs Skill Council for Green Jobs \n33 PwD Skill Council for Persons with Disability \n34 Domestic Workers Domestic Workers Sector Skill Council \n35 Furniture & Fittings Furniture & Fittings Skill Council \n36 Instrumentation Instrumentation, Automation, Surveillance & Communi cation \nSector Skill Council \n\n37 Management  Management & Entrepreneurship and Professional Skills Council \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_417": " \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 417 RAISED BY SHRI JANARDAN SINGH \nSIGRIWAL, HON’BLE MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT TO BE ANSWERED ON \n23RD MARCH 2020 REGARDING FUNDS FOR KENDRIYA VIDYALAYAS.  \n \n(a) All construction works of Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan (KVS) are \nexecuted on “Deposit Work” basis from concept to commissioning stage through \nGovernment construction agencies viz. Central Public Works Department \n(CPWD), Military Engineer Services (MES), Railways, State Public Works \nDepartments (PWD), Central / State Public Sector Undertakings. Administrative \nApproval and Expenditure Sanction (AA&ES) is issued by KVS on the basis of \napproved preliminary drawings as per KVS norms and preliminary estimate \nsubmitted by construction agencies. Funds are released in instalments based on \nprogress of work for which monthly progress reports in the prescribed format \nalong with photographs are submitted by the construction agencies duly certified \nby the Principal concerned.  \n \n(b) KVS has informed that no such case has been reported, so far.  \n \n(c) & (d) Separate toilet facility for girl students is available in good condition in all \nthe Kendriya Vidyalayas.  \n \n****** ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_418": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 418   \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 23.03.2020 \n \nTRADITIONAL TRIBAL ART AND CULTURE PROGRAMME UNDER PMKVY \n \n† *418. SHRI RAJENDRA DHEDYA GAVIT: \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP \nbe pleased to state : \n \n(a) whether the Government is implementing any sche me in Maharashtra which \nincludes traditional tribal art in the training pro gramme under the Pradhan Mantri \nKaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY); and \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER IN THE MINISTRY OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(DR. MAHENDRA NATH PANDEY) \n \n(a) and (b) A Statement is laid on the Table of the  House.   \n  \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) AND (B)  OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 418 TO BE ANSWERED ON 23.03.20 20 ASKED BY \nSHRI RAJENDRA DHEDYA GAVIT  REGARDING TRADITIONAL TRIBAL ART \nAND CULTURE PROGRAMME UNDER PMKVY  \n \n(a) and (b)  Ministry of Skill Development and Entr epreneurship is implementing \nPradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) (2016-2 0) for imparting short \nduration skill development training under the compo nent of Short Term Training \n(STT) and Recognition of Prior Learning (RPL) in th e country including state of \nMaharashtra. Under PMKVY (2016-20), training is bei ng imparted in more than 1800 \njob roles of 38 different sectors including various  job roles of traditional arts and \ncrafts. Under the scheme, provisions have been made to promote traditional arts and \ncrafts in the country through imparting training in  this sector. Such provision includes \nthat State/UTs have been given flexibility to alloc ate upto 25% of their total allocated \ntarget for imparting skill training in State specif ic job roles and the sector of local \ntraditional arts and crafts.  \n \nUnder PMKVY (2016-20), till now, 73,667 candidates have been \ntrained/oriented (4,667 trained under STT and 69,000 oriented under RPL) in various \ntraditional job roles in the country. These job rol es include like carpet weaving, \ncarving artisans, beading artisans, bamboo mat weav er, tarakashi jeweller, \ndecorative painter, sketching & painting artisans, fashion jewellery, crochet Lace \ntrailers, hand embroiderer etc. Out of these, 1093 candidates have been trained in \nState of Maharashtra under job role ‘Crochet Lace Trailers’ of Handicrafts sector.  \n \nAdditionally, Under Jan Shikhan Sansthan (JSS) Sche me, training in warli \npainting is being imparted in the State of Maharashtra.   \n \n******* ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_419": " \n \n \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Consumer Affairs, Food and Public Distribution \nDepartment of Consumer Affairs \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 419 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2020 \n \nSUPPLY OF IMPORTED ONIONS \n \n419. SHRI SRIDHAR KOTAGIRI: SHRI N. REDDEPPA: SHRI ADALA \nPRABHAKARA REDDY: SHRI CHANDRA SEKHAR BELLANA:  \n \nWill the Minister of CONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC \nDISTRIBUTION miHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k ea=h be \npleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has offered to supply imported onions to State \nGovernments at Rs. 49 to Rs. 58 per kg recently;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) the States which have purchased onions from these imported stocks and the \ndetails thereof; and  \n(d)  the total amount spent by the Government on these imports? \n \nANSWER \n \nmiHkksDrk ekeys] [kk| vkSj lkoZtfud forj.k jkT; ea=h  \n¼Jh nkuos jkolkgsc nknkjko½ \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE  \nCONSUMER AFFAIRS, FOOD AND PUBLIC DISTRIBUTION \n(SHRI DANVE RAOSAHEB DADARAO) \n \n(a)  & (b) : Government had earlier offered/ supplied imported onions at cost price \nwhich is now offered/supplied to States at prevailing market/mandi/online portal \nrates.  \n \n(c)    : The details of imported onion supplied to various States/UTs is at \nAnnexure. \n \n(d)        : As on 31.01.2020, MMTC has placed a demand of Rs. 226 crore towards \nimports of onion. \n \n*****   \n\n \n \n \n \nANNEXURE  \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED IN REPLY TO PART (c) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 419 FOR 04.02.2020 REGARDING SUPPLY OF IMPORTED \nONIONS. \n \nDispatch of imported onion to States/UTs \n  \n                                                                                                          (As on 30.01.2020) \nS.No. States/UTs Quantity (in MT) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 893.18 \n2 Kerala 49.89 \n3 Telangana 111.68 \n4 Uttar Pradesh 211.79 \n5 Uttarakhand 262.60 \n6 West Bengal 123.19 \n7 Himachal Pradesh 120.64 \n8 Assam 190.27 \n9 Goa 50.31 \n10 Jammu & Kashmir 45.71 \n11 Haryana 218.60 \n12 Meghalaya 282.59 \n13 Odisha 48.50 \n Total 2608.95 \nSource : NAFED \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_420": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 420 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 4TH FEBRUARY, 2020/ MAGHA 15, 1941 (SAKA) \n \nJNU INCIDENT \n \n420.  SHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB: \nSHRI HIBI EDEN: \nSHRI N.K. PREMACHANDRAN: \nSHRI DEEPAK BAIJ: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government has conducted inquiry on attack against the \nstudents and teachers of JNU on 5th January, 2020 by masked people \nwith rods and sticks; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the number of students \nkilled/injured and damage to public property; \n \n(c) whether the Government has registered FIR against the culprits and \narrest them and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) the safety measures taken by the Government to protect the JNU \ncampus from such attacks; \n \n(e) whether the police registered cases against the injured students, if so, \nthe details thereof and the reasons therefor; \n \n(f) whether any outsiders participated in the mask attack in JNU, if so, the \ndetails thereof and the action taken against them; and \n \n(g) whether the Government proposes to conduct an independent enquiry \nto ascertain failure of police to prevent the attack and if so, the details \nthereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n\n-2- \n \nL.S.US.Q.NO.420 FOR 04.02.2020 \n \n \n(a) to (c): As reported by Delhi Police, a case has been registered at PS \nVasant Kunj North on 6th January, 2020 with regard to the attack against \nthe students and teachers of Jawaharlal Nehru University (JNU) on 5th \nJanuary 2020 by masked people with rods and sticks.  51 persons \nsustained injuries and all were medically examined.  No one was killed in \nthis incident.  Some private cars and property were also damaged.  Some \nof the rioters involved have been identified. \n \n(d): The safety measures taken by Delhi Police include deployment of \nPolice personnel both inside and outside the JNU Campus, liaison with \nstudents and University Administration to maintain peace, deployment of \nPolice personnel in plain clothes around the Campus, stationing of PCR \nVan in the vicinity of JNU Campus and briefing of students and \nAdministration to report to Police immediately, if any violent/ unwanted \nactivities come to notice in the premises of the Campus.  JNU has \ninformed that they have deployed 277 private security personnel 24x7 in \nJNU Campus.   \n \n(e) to (g): As reported by Delhi Police, no case has been registered by \nDelhi Police against the injured students.  Details of investigation cannot \nbe divulged at this stage.    \n******* ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_421": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, COOPERATION AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nLOK  SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n421\n                     \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE  \n4\nTH\n \nFEBRUARY,\n \n20\n20\n \n \nSOCIETY FOR WELFARE SCHEMES\n \n \n421. \n \nSHRI MOHAMMED FAIZAL P.P.: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण \nमं\u0000ी\n \nbe pleased to state:\n \n \n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether the Government has formed any society to run all the Centrally sponsored\n \nfarmer welfare schemes; \n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has found different methods to improve monitoring and \ntargeting on farmers schemes; and \n \n \n(d) \n \nif so, details thereof?\n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \nकृ\u0000ष\n \nएवं \n\u0000कसान \nक\u0000याण\n \nमं\u0000ी\n  \n   \n       \n( SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR)\n  \n \n \n(a)  \n&  \n \n(b)\n:\n \nA National Farmer’s Welfare Programme Implementation Society has been \nregistered on 23.12.2019 to operate certain Central Sector Schemes related to farmers’ \nwelfare.\n \n \n(c) & (d)\n:\n \n \nThe Department regularly monitors the progress of schemes through meetings \nwith concerned officers of the State Governments/UTs, visits of nodal officers of the \nDepartment to the States/UTs, video conferencing, Rabi and Kharif Conferences, etc.  \nBesides t\nhe beneficiary details of different schemes of the Department are uploaded in the \nDirect Benefit Transfer (DBT) portal for monitoring and tracking of beneficiaries, etc.  Further, \nfinancial assistance extended to the beneficiary is directly credited into t\nheir bank accounts \nthrough the DBT mode.\n \n \n \n******\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_422": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 422 \nANSWERED ON 04.02.2020 \n \nDECLINE IN SALE OF CARS \n \n422. SHRI DIBYENDU ADHIKARI: \n        PROF. SAUGATA RAY: \n \nWill the Minister of HEAVY INDUSTRIES AND  PUBLIC ENTERPRISES  भारी \nउद्योग एवं ऱोक उद्यम मंत्री be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that the sale of car in the country has dipped over 60 per \ncent in the last seven months period, if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor; \n \n(b) whether the Government is also aware that the  private car manufacturers have started \nretrenchment of workers in the country; \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the action taken by the Government thereon; \n \n(d) the proposal of the Government on their commitment of creating employment therein; and \n \n(e) the steps being taken by the Government to increase the automobile sale in the country? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF HEAVY INDUSTRIES & PUBLIC ENTERPRISES \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n \n(a) & (b):  During the last seven months (June – December 2019) the sale of Passenger \nVehicles has declined to 1.6 million from 1.9 million during the same period in 2018. \nRetrenchment of temporary workforce has been reported by the industry. However, no \nconfirmed data on job loss is available with the Government. \n \n(c) to (e):  The Government, as a policymaker, always attempts to keep and improve \nmomentum of the economy through a package of measure for comprehensive and continued \ndevelopment of the auto sector as and when required. Some of the steps taken by the \nGovernment to counter automotive slowdown can be summarized as under: \n Reduction in Corporate Tax to 22% \n Continuation of registration of ICE and EV in future \n Scrappage policy under consideration \n Proposed increase in registration of new cars deferred till June 2020 \n Funds worth Rs. 70,000 crores released to PSU banks  \n Linking of repo rate to interest charged for vehicle purchased  \n********** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_423": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. †423 \nANSWERED ON 04TH FEBRUARY, 2020 \n \nAGRO-BASED INDUSTRIES \n \n†423. SHRI RAVINDRA KUSHWAHA: \n \nWill the Minister of FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether any scheme to set up agro-based new industries in the country is under the \nconsideration of the Government; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to set up agro-based industries in the Northern \nStates including Uttar Pradesh; and \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES  \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n \n(a) to (d): The Ministry of Food Processing Industries is already implementing a Central Sector \nUmbrella Scheme – PRADHAN MANTRI KISAN SAMPADA YOJANA - (PMKSY) with \nan allocation of Rs.6000 crore for the period 2016 -20 with the scheme components viz: (i) \nMega Food Parks, (ii) Integrated Cold Chain and Value Addition Infrastructure, (iii) \nInfrastructure for Agro -processing Clusters, (iv) Creation of Backward and Forward Linkages, \n(v) Creation/Expansion of Food Processing & Preservation Capacities, (vi) Food Safety and \nQuality Assurance Infrastructure and (vii) Human Resources and Institutions for setting up of \nvarious food processing industries/projects/units in the country for preservation and processing \nof various agro-produce such as cereals, vegetables, f ruits, milk, fish, poultry & meat etc. in the \ncountry including in the Northern States and  Uttar  Pradesh. The Ministry is also implementing \nanother Central Sector Scheme \"Operation Greens\" under PMKSY since November 2018 for \nintegrated development of val ue/supply chain of Tomato, Onion and Potato (TOP) crops in \nselected States on pilot basis that includes the State of Uttar Pradesh. The Government does not \nset up any food processing industries/projects/units on its own. Under the schemes of PMKSY \nfinancial assistance in the form grants -in-aid is provided to farmers, entrepreneurs, \norganizations such as Central and State PSUs/Joint Ventures/Farmer Producer Organizations \n(FPOs)/NGOs/Cooperatives/SHGs/ Public and Private Companies etc. to set up food processi ng \nindustries/projects/units. These Schemes are demand driven. Financial assistance is provided to \nthe eligible applicant from all parts of the country including the Northern States and Uttar \nPradesh as per the Scheme guidelines and against the Expression of Interest issued by the \nMinistry from time to time. \n \n \n \n*****\n\n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_424": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY & DAIRYING \nDEPARTMENT OF ANIMAL HUSBANDRY & DAIRYING  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 424 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 4TH FEBRUARY, 2020 \n \nHORMONAL INJECTION FOR INCREASING PRODUCTION OF \nMILK AND EGGS \n \n424. SHRIMATI MEENAKASHI LEKHI    \nWill the Minister of FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY & DAIRYING  \nमत्स्यपालन, पशुपालन और डेयरी मंत्री  \nbe pleased to state: \n(a) Whether it is true that to increase production of milk and eggs, the h ormonal injections \nare given to animals \n(b) If so, the details thereof; \n(c) Whether such injections will affect the human body after consumption of those \nproducts; \n(d) Whether any research or study has been undertaken to make the process more organic; \nand \n(e) If so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor? \n \n ANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FISHERIES, ANIMAL HUSBANDRY & DAIRYING \n(DR. SANJEEV KUMAR BALYAN) \n \n(a) to (b) No Sir. There is no documentary evidence available with the Department regarding \nuse of hormonal injections to increase production of milk  and eggs. However, use of \noxytocin has been reported for letdown of milk for which Department has periodically \nissued advisories to create awareness among dairy owners regarding ill effects of non -\njudicious use of oxytocin. \n \n        (c) No such information is available with the Department. \n \n        (d) to (e) No such information is available with the Department.    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_425": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 425 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 4TH FEBRUARY, 2020/ MAGHA 15, 1941 (SAKA) \n \nKEEPING NPR ON HOLD \n \n425.  ADV. ADOOR PRAKASH: \nSHRI PRASUN BANERJEE: \nSHRI ANUMULA REVANTH REDDY: \n \nWill the Minister of HOME AFFAIRS be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that some States including Kerala \nhave put the works related to updating National Population Register (NPR) \non hold; \n \n(b) if so, the response of the Government thereto; \n \n(c) whether the Government has finalized the questionnaire for National \nPopulation Register; \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(e) the details of documents mandatorily required for updating NPR; \n \n(f) whether the database of NPR will be used for National Register of \nCitizens; and \n \n(g) if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS \n(SHRI NITYANAND RAI) \n \n(a) & (b): The Government is in discussion with the States having \nconcerns in regard to the preparation of National Population Register \n(NPR). \n\n \n-2- \nL.S.US.Q.NO.425 FOR 04.02.2020 \n (c) to (e): The demographic and other particulars of each family and \nindividual are to be updated/collected during the exercise of updation of \nNPR. No document is to be collected during this exercise. \n \n(f) & (g): Till now, the Government has not taken any decision to \nprepare National Register of Indian Citizens (NRIC) at the National level. \n \n************* ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_426": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 426 \nANSWERED ON 04TH FEBRUARY, 2020 \n \nBENEFITS OF MEGA FOOD PARKS \n \n426. SHRI PRADEEP KUMAR SINGH: \nSHRIMATI RATHVA GITABEN VAJESINGBHAI: \nSHRI NARANBHAI KACHHADIYA: \nSHRI SHANTANU THAKUR: \n \nWill the Minister of FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES be pleased to state: \n \n(a) Whether farmers are gradually getting benefits through Mega Food Parks, if so,  the \ndetails thereof; \n \n(b) the details and total number of Mega Food Parks that are operational in country; \n \n(c) whether the Government is planning to open new Mega Food Parks in different States of \ncountry and also in Bihar, Gujarat and West Bengal, if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(d) whether Mega Food Parks to create employments and job opportunities, if so,  the details \nthereof the last three years? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n \n(a), (b) & (d) : As per Mega Food Park scheme guidelines, each Mega Food Park on being fully \noperational will create direct / indirect employment of about 5,000 persons and also benefit about \n25,000 farmers. However, the actual configuration of the project may vary dependi ng upon the \nbusiness plan for each Mega Food Park. Presently, Ministry has accorded final approval to 39 \nMega Food Park Projects which are under various stages of implementation. Out of these, a total \nof 18 Mega Food Park projects at Haridwar (Uttarakhand) , Chittoor (Andhra Pradesh), Tumkur \n(Karnataka), Fazilka (Punjab), Nalbari (Assam), Khargone (Madhya Pradesh), Murshidabad \n(West Bengal), Rayagada (Odisha), Satara (Maharashtra), Ajmer (Rajasthan), Udham Singh \nNagar (Uttarakhand), Surat (Gujarat), Aurangab ad (Maharashtra), Una (HP), West Godavari \n(Andhra Pradesh), West Tripura (Tripura), Nizamabad (Telangana) and Dewas (Madhya \nPradesh) have been made operational. Details of actual employment generated from the 11 Mega \nFood Parks made operational during last three years are at Annexure. \n \n(c):  Ministry of Food Processing Industries has been implementing Mega Food Park Scheme \n(MFPS) to create modern infrastructure for the food processing. Ministry does not establish \nMega Food Parks in the country on its own. The proposals under Mega Food Park Scheme for \nsetting up of Mega Food Parks in the country are  invited through Expression of Interest (EoI) \nfrom time to time. Selection of suitable proposals for these projects is done as per the Scheme \nguidelines, based on the merit, through a three tier stringent appraisal process as per the prefixed \ncriteria. At present, Ministry has not invited any EoI for submission of proposals under the \nScheme. As on date, there is no proposal under consideration to establish any  new Mega Food \nParks in Bihar, Gujarat and West Bengal under the Mega Food Park Scheme of the Ministry. \n \n***** \n\n \n \n \nANNEXURE \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART ( a), (b ) & ( d) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 426 FOR ANSWER ON 04 TH FEBRUARY, 2020 REGARDING “BENEFITS OF MEGA \nFOOD PARKS”. \n \nDetails of actual employment generated from the 11 Mega Food Parks operationalised  during last three \nyears \n \nSl. \nNo. \nName of SPV/IA of \nMFP project \n \nDistrict & State \nDate of \nOperationalization \nActual \nEmployment \nGenerated (Nos.) \n1. MITS Mega Food Park Ltd Rayagada, Odisha 1-Jun-2017 2124 \n2. Satara Mega Food Park Pvt \nLtd \nSatara, Maharshtra 1-Mar-2018 229 \n3. Greentech Mega Food \nPark Ltd \nAjmer, Rajasthan 29-Mar-2018 300 \n \n4. \n \nHimalayan Food Park Pvt \nLtd \nUdham Singh \nNagar, \nUttarakhand \n \n8-Apr-2018 \n \n16040 \n \n5. \nGujarat Agro \nInfrastructure Mega \nFood Park Pvt Ltd \nSurat, Gujarat 29-Oct-2018  \n600 \n \n6. \nPaithan Mega Food \nPark Pvt Ltd \nAurangabad, \nMaharashtra \n15-Nov-2018  \n408 \n \n7. \nCremica Food Park Pvt Ltd Una, Himachal \nPradesh \n10-Feb-2019  \n600 \n \n8. \nGodavari Mega Aqua \nFood Park Pvt Ltd \nWest Godavari, \nAndhra Pradesh \n12-Feb-2019  \n250 \n \n9. \nSikaria Mega Food Park \n(P) Ltd \nWest Tripura, \nTripura \n20-Feb-2019  \n300 \n \n10. \nSmart Agro Food Park Pvt \nLtd \nNizamabad, \nTelangana \n6-Sep-2019  \n125 \n \n11. \nAvantee Mega Food \nPark Pvt Ltd \nDewas, Madhya \nPradesh \n5-Dec-2019  \n200 \n \nNote:- Food Processing Industries Being Seasonal In Nature, The Above Figures May Change From Time \nTo Time. \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_427": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES  \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 427 \nANSWERED ON 04TH FEBRUARY, 2020 \n \nIMPLEMENTATION OF CEFPPC SCHEME \n \n427. SHRI REBATI TRIPURA: \nSHRI DHANUSH M. KUMAR: \nSHRI SOYAM BAPU RAO: \nSHRI SELVAM G.: \nSHRI GAUTAM SIGAMAANI PON: \nDR. HEENA GAVIT: \n \nWill the Minister of FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is implementing the Creation/Expansion of Food Processing and \nPreservation Capacities (CEFPPC) scheme,  if so, the present status and the achievement \nby the scheme since its inception especially, State-wise; \n \n(b) whether an Inter -Ministerial Approval Committee (IMAC) has approved project worth \nRs. 271 crore under the CEFPPC scheme, if so, the details thereof an d the criteria fixed \nfor this purpose; \n \n(c) whether the Government is focusing on projects that emphasized on linking agriculture \nand marketing food processing technologies, if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether the Government has set any target in the scheme for generation of employment, \nif so, the details thereof; and \n \n(e) the other steps taken/being taken by the Government in linking agriculture and marketing \nfood processing technologies? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR FOOD PROCESSING INDUSTRIES \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n \n(a):  Yes Sir. Ministry of Food Processing Industries (MoFPI) is implementing a Scheme for \nCreation/Expansion of Food Processing & Preservation Capacities (CEFPPC) under the Pradhan  \nMantri Kisan Sampada Yojana (PMKSY) for creation/expansion of food processing industries in \nthe country. As on date, 219 food processing units have been approved under the scheme since inception. \nThe state-wise number of units approved, grants -in-aid sanctioned and released under the scheme is a t \nAnnexure-I. \n \n(b):  Intern-Ministerial Approval Committee (IMAC) has approved 219 projects under the \nscheme in the country till date with total project cost of Rs. 2989.18 Crore including grant-in- aid \nof Rs. 821.41 crore. The criteria prescribed in the scheme guidelines date d 08.01.2020 for \nevaluation / selection of the proposals is at Annexure-II. \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n(c):  MoFPI gives additional weightage to projects focusing on adoption of modern / \ninnovative food processing technologies and also utilization of perishable agriculture prod uce by \nthe units. \n \n(d):  The Government has approved a target of 85,000 direct & indirect employment under the \nscheme for 400 food processing units during 14th Finance Commission cycle. \n \n(e):  MoFPI is also implementing Mega Food Parks (MFPs) and Agro Processing Clusters \n(APCs) schemes which aim at providing modern infrastructure facilities for the food processing \nalong the value chain from the farm to the market based on the cluster approach. This w ill result \nin setting up of more food processing units in agricultural production clusters. \n \n***** \n\n \n \n \n \nANNEXURE-I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED  TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION \nNO. 427 FOR ANSWER ON 04TH FEBRUARY, 2020  REGARDING “IMPLEMENTATION OF \nCEFPPC SCHEME” \n \nDetails of State -wise approved food processing units and grants -in-aid sanctioned / released under the \nScheme for Creation / Expansion of Food Processing & Preservation Capacities (CEFPPC) of Pradhan \nMantri Kisan Sampada Yojana (PMKSY) as on 30.01.2020 \n \nSl. \nNo \nState No. of units \napproved \nAmount of Grant-in-Aid \nApproved \n(Rs. in Crore) \nAmount of Grant \nReleased \n(Rs. in Crore) \n1 Andhra Pradesh 2 8.48 0.00 \n2 Arunachal \nPradesh \n1 5.00 0.00 \n3 Assam 4 16.89 6.90 \n4 Bihar 1 5.00 0.00 \n5 Chhatisgarh 1 5.00 2.50 \n6 Goa 1 2.90 0.00 \n7 Gujarat 24 94.15 5.93 \n8 Haryana 15 55.01 13.65 \n9 Himachal \nPradesh \n16 52.42 11.08 \n10 Jammu & \nKashmir \n16 51.55 7.34 \n11 Jharkhand 0 0.00 0.00 \n12 Karnataka 11 33.36 6.77 \n13 Kerala 9 32.74 4.60 \n14 Madhya Pradesh 7 32.86 12.36 \n15 Maharashtra 29 93.82 13.46 \n16 Manipur 0 0.00 0.00 \n17 Meghalaya 1 1.36 1.36 \n18 Mizoram 1 2.04 0.00 \n19 Nagaland 4 19.87 9.94 \n20 Odisha 2 10.00 7.50 \n21 Punjab 5 21.21 11.10 \n22 Rajasthan 9 29.34 9.89 \n23 Sikkim 1 5.00 0.00 \n24 Tamil Nadu 19 72.44 31.30 \n25 Telangana 2 9.29 0.00 \n26 Tripura 2 10.00 0.00 \n27 Uttar Pradesh 19 78.88 32.50 \n28 Uttarakhand 11 50.49 0.00 \n29 West Bengal 6 22.31 3.17 \n30 A&N Islands 0 0.00 0.00 \n31 Chandigarh 0 0.00 0.00 \n32 D&N Haveli 0 0.00 0.00 \n33 Delhi 0 0.00 0.00 \n34 Daman & Diu 0 0.00 0.00 \n35 Lakshdweep 0 0.00 0.00 \n36 Pondicherry 0 0.00 0.00 \n Total 219 821.41 191.35 \n\n \n \nANNEXURE-II \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART  (b) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 427 FOR \nANSWER ON 04TH FEBRUARY, 2020 REGARDING “IMPLEMENTATION OF CEFPPC SCHEME” \n \nCriteria for evaluation of proposals under Scheme for creation of food Processing & Preservation capacities \n Sl. \nNo. Criteria for Evaluation of the proposal Marks Max \nmarks \nModifications approved by \nIMAC \n1 Priority Sector       \na. For Perishable Products (Fruits &Veg, Meat & Poultry, Milk & Aqua \nProducts etc.) \n20 \n20 DPR/ Bank appraisal and IEM b. For Consumer products (Bakery/Snacks/Breakfast cereals/RTE \nproducts etc.) \n10 \nc. For Non- Perishable Products (Grain/Pulse/Oil milling etc.) 05 \n2 Leveraging of Investment in the project       \nFor General areas   \n15   \nDPR/ Bank appraisal \na. Proposed private investment including equity and unsecured loan >= \n1.5 times of grant sought \n15 \nb. Proposed private investment including equity and unsecured loan < \n1.5 times of grant sought \n10 \nFor SC/ST, NER/ Himalayan States, Island areas& ITDP areas.   \na. Proposed private investment including equity and unsecured loan >= \ngrant sought \n15 \nb. Proposed private investment including equity and unsecured loan < \ngrant sought \n10 \n3 Investment on Eligible Project cost       \na. More than Rs.15 crore 12 \n12 DPR/ CE Certificate. b. More than Rs 9 crore to 15 crore 08 \nc. Between Rs. 3 crore to 9 crore 06 \nd. Below Rs. 3 crore (in case of SC/ST, NER/Himalayan \nStates/ITDP/Island ) \n04     \n4 Net worth of the applicant       \n  a. More than 2 times of proposed equity  05          \n05 Balance Sheet / CA Certificate / \nSupporting Documents b. 1.5 to 2 times of proposed equity 03 \nc.. Less than 1.5 times of proposed equity 0 \n5 Debt Service Coverage Ratio (DSCR) based on Bank appraisal       \n  a. 3.0 and above 07 \n07 Bank Appraisal Report \nb. Between 2.5 but less than 3.0 05 \nc. Between 2.0 but less than 2.5 03 \nd. Between 1.5 but less than 2.0 01 \ne. Less than 1.5 00 \n6 Women entrepreneur(s)        \n  \na. 100% shareholding of women in the firm 05 \n05 Relevant documents / ROC b. Majority stake / shareholding (more than 50% and less than 100% of \nwomen in the firm) \n02 \n7 Project Strength - The promoter(s) having professional / special   \ntraining in food processing / technology \n      \n  a. M.Tech / Ph.D. in Food Processing / Technology 05 \n05 Copy of Degree / Diploma / \nCertificate \nb. B.Tech in Food Processing / Technology 04 \nc. Diploma in Food Processing / Technology 03 \nd. Special Training in Food Processing / Technology for a period not \nless six months from Govt. recognized University / Institute 02 \n8 Experience of applicant firm / promoter(s) in Food Processing:        \n  \na. Food processing business having annual turnover of ₹3 crore and \nabove during previous year 10 \n10 Balance sheet, FSSAI license \netc. \nb. Food processing business having annual turnover of ₹2 crore but less \nthan ₹3 crore above during previous year 7 \nc. Food processing business having annual turnover of ₹1 crore but less \nthan ₹2 crore  during previous year 5 \nd. Food processing business having annual turnover of less than ₹1 \ncrore during the previous year 3     \n9 Introduction of innovative technology /